swer\n\n### Concept\n<!-- What it is — the essential definition or idea in 1–3 sentences -->\n\n### Mechanism\n<!-- How it works — the steps, architecture, algorithm, or process -->\n\n### Example / Tradeoff\n<!-- A concrete system, metric, or comparison that makes the answer real.\n     Include real tools/systems: FAISS, Pinecone, RAGAS, LoRA, HNSW, vLLM, LangChain, etc. -->\n\n---\n\n## Verbal script\n\n<!-- 3–5 minute spoken outline. First-person, interview voice.\n     Openers: \"I'd start by…\", \"The key insight here is…\", \"A concrete example is…\" -->\n\n**Opening (30s):**\n<!-- Frame the question and signal your approach -->\n\n**Core explanation (2–3 min):**\n<!-- Walk through concept → mechanism → example -->\n\n**Tradeoff / production angle (1 min):**\n<!-- When does this approach break down? What would you do differently at scale? -->\n\n**Wrap-up (30s):**\n<!-- Summarize the key point and invite follow-up -->\n\n---\n\n## Pitfalls\n\n<!-- ≥2 concrete mistakes weak candidates make. Format: Mistake → Better.\n     Be specific: \"Saying 'just use GPT-4' without discussing cost, latency, or vendor lock-in\"\n     NOT \"doesn't think about alternatives\" -->\n- **Mistake:** <!-- what they say/skip --> — **Better:** <!-- what to say instead -->\n- **Mistake:** <!-- what they say/skip --> — **Better:** <!-- what to say instead -->\n\n---\n\n## Related questions\n\n<!-- 2–3 cross-links. Use relative paths within ai-engineering/answers/.\n     Cross-category links are valid. Format: [Q text](NN-QQQ-slug.md) -->\n| Question | Relationship |\n|----------|--------------|\n| [<!-- Q text -->](<!-- NN-QQQ-slug.md -->) | <!-- prerequisite / follow-up / same concept --> |\n| [<!-- Q text -->](<!-- NN-QQQ-slug.md -->) | |\n\n---\n\n## One-liner recall\n\n<!-- Single sentence. Should let you reconstruct the full answer from memory. -->\n\n> <!-- Your one-liner here -->\n","numLines":86,"startLine":1,"totalLines":86}}}
