{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01NAgkzwPUPCESbBGNa6dyJC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q13 — Common RAG failure points — how debug them?**\n\n---\n\n**Core framework: the 6 canonical failure modes**\n\n| # | Failure | Stage | Diagnostic |\n|---|---------|-------|------------|\n| 1 | Bad chunking | Ingest | `context_recall` low; chunks split mid-table/mid-argument |\n| 2 | Vocabulary mismatch | Retrieval | Dense misses exact entity names (SKUs, codes, names) |\n| 3 | Lost in the middle | Generation | Retrieved docs are right but answer is wrong; gold doc in positions 2–4 |\n| 4 | Hallucination on absent context | Generation | `faithfulness` < 0.7; model answers despite no relevant passage |\n| 5 | Stale index / embedding drift | Index | Source has correct answer; vector store has old version |\n| 6 | Weak evaluation | Eval | Vibes-based review hides retrieval failures until production complaints |\n\n**Debug protocol:** Run RAGAS first — if `context_recall` < 0.7, the retrieval is broken (fix that before touching generation); if `faithfulness` < 0.7 with good recall, the generation is the problem. Log 20–50 failing queries to inspect top-5 chunks manually and identify which subtype you're dealing with.\n\n**Key pitfall covered:** Jumping to prompt-tuning or a bigger model when `context_recall` is actually the issue — fluent hallucinations are the worst outcome of weak eval."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":347,"cache_read_input_tokens":63259,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":347,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4dabb1ab-9c09-4fd8-923f-61b61a174726","uuid":"2a9ddee6-bf98-46fd-9efd-045c417c2852"}
